The sketches in this directory are stock Arduino-ESP32 programs. Each uses ordinary Arduino
calls and nothing else. They were compiled with Arduino CLI 1.5.1 and esp32:esp32 3.3.12, fqbn
esp32:esp32:esp32s3, which is the ESP32S3 Dev Module defaults: USB CDC on boot disabled, PSRAM
disabled, 4MB flash, the default partition table, QIO 80MHz, and the sketch on core 1. The core
is not kept here. Its package is LGPL-2.1-or-later. The HAL files it builds with are Apache-2.0.
The prebuilt libraries under esp32s3-libs are ESP-IDF's, under the terms named in
packages/engine/tests/firmware/esp32s3/idf/NOTICE.
Every app also links Mbed TLS objects (sha.c, platform.c and platform_util.c from
libmbedcrypto.a), Copyright The Mbed TLS Contributors, which ESP-IDF carries under Apache-2.0 OR
GPL-2.0-or-later, used here under the Apache License 2.0.

The compile rewrites source paths with -ffile-prefix-map, the same way
packages/engine/scripts/esp32s3-arduino.sh does, so the committed app does not record the build
directory. A sketch built without that map is the same program with different path strings.

The app and the partition table are kept in the scene fixture named below, as app.bin and
partitions.bin. The partition table is the core's default 4MB table, the same bytes for every
sketch. The bootloader and the merged image are not kept. The chip starts where the bootloader
leaves the app.

Each fixture's partitions.bin is the same file: 3072 bytes,
148b959cbff1c38aa8e1d5c0ba9d612c54997b945e56a63f41223eef650653a1.

